  "body": "Found while fixing #994 (the mill canned-cycle posts traversing at R).\n\n**What is wrong.** `fanuc-lathe.cps` (and `tormach-lathe.cps` should be checked the same way) swallows every rapid after a face-drilling cycle until the section ends, so the chain's exit rapid to clearance never posts. The tool leaves the hole at the cycle's initial level (= R, the positioning rapid stands there) and the next motion is the home move. The committed golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/axial_drill.nc` (from `lathe_post.rs`, clearance 30, R 20) shows it:\n\n```\nG00 X0 Z20\nG83 Z10 Q12000 F0.008\nG80\nM9\nM05\nG28 U0 W0        <- from Z20 (R); the verified path first rises to Z30\n```\n\nA lathe drills a single on-axis hole, so there is no traverse between holes. But the exit is lower than the verified motion, and `G28 U0 W0` moves X and Z together from there.\n\n**Done means:** the lathe posts leave a face-drilling cycle at the stream's exit level. #994's law fits here too: the first rapid that leaves the hole ends the group (`G80`) and posts as the stream says. Pin it with the `axial_drill` goldens and a read-back assertion, like `crates/post/tests/cycle_hop.rs` from #994.\n",
